From e2456248ee43d77392d379e8f0182cac8b8ac301 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:47:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0172: one-time read-only shop probe at the list NrvDecide
 confirm

A FRAME_STEP cut at 0x2e8dfc (mov x22, x0) dumps, per list confirm,
the list's 0x70 bytes, the [list+0x30] layout object (0x1b8 bytes,
incl. [A+0x68] and the [A+0x70] selection-gate float), the [list+0x38]
container (0x60 bytes) and the 0x50a5c0 return (x22, 0x80 bytes) into
the probe buffer at state +0x3300 (magic SH72, len at +0x08, fire at
+0x0c -- +0x04 is reserved: dm_hud_probe_tick writes 0 there every
present, which zeroed 0164's len). The host drain logs one [shop] line
set per confirm with the fire sequence number. Read-only: the stub
writes only the probe buffer, reproduces the replaced mov x22, x0 in
the trampoline, and never touches game memory or the buy flow. This is
NOT the 0164 hook (0x442664 required the name to be exactly
ectionMap and never fired at a real buy); 0x442664 is not reused.
User-approved 2026-11-17 18:39 as a single one-time exception to the
probe ban; delete from series after the device run reads the row.
